@startuml sequence
!include style.puml
title One research run - sequence diagram
autonumber "<b>0."
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
boundary "Streamlit UI\n<size:10>app.py</size>" as ui
control "Pipeline\n<size:10>pipeline.py</size>" as pipe
box "Agent roles" #F5F6FC
  participant "Researcher\n<size:10>researcher.py</size>" as res
  participant "Verifier\n<size:10>verifier.py</size>" as ver
  participant "Writer + Critic\n<size:10>writer.py</size>" as wri
end box
collections "Tools\n<size:10>search.py, fetch.py</size>\n<size:10>credibility.py</size>" as tools
participant "Gemini API" as gem #FFF3E0
participant "PDF builder\n<size:10>pdf_report.py</size>" as pdf
database "Run folder\n<size:10>runs/<id>/</size>" as disk

user -> ui : enter topic + depth
ui -> pipe : run(topic, depth)

== 1. Plan ==
pipe -> gem : planner prompt + JSON schema
gem --> pipe : 5-8 research questions with search queries

== 2. Research (agent loop) ==
pipe -> res : questions + source budget
loop until each question has enough good sources, or the step budget is used up
  res -> gem : conversation history + tool list
  gem --> res : function call, e.g. web_search(query)
  res -> tools : run the tool
  tools --> res : results with trust tier
  res -> gem : tool result, marked as untrusted data
end
res --> pipe : scored sources
pipe --> ui : live progress events

== 3. Extract ==
pipe -> gem : source text, extract claims (gemini-3.1-flash-lite)
gem --> pipe : claim + supporting quote + source id
pipe -> pipe : keep a claim only if its quote is in the source

== 4. Cross-validate ==
pipe -> ver : all claims
ver -> gem : embed claims (gemini-embedding-2)
ver -> gem : does each source agree or contradict?
ver -> ver : count independent websites, give labels
alt some claims are unverified
  ver -> tools : targeted search (web + OpenAlex)
  tools --> ver : new tier 1-2 sources
  ver -> gem : extract and check that question again
end
ver --> pipe : confidence label per claim group

== 5. Write ==
pipe -> wri : verified + likely claims
wri -> gem : one section per question, then the summary
wri -> wri : critic removes sentences without a source
wri --> pipe : report sections (JSON)

== 6. Publish ==
pipe -> pdf : sections, sources, charts
pdf -> disk : report.pdf
pipe -> disk : state.json + trace.jsonl
pipe --> ui : finished
ui --> user : PDF preview + download
@enduml
